================================================================================
SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER
================================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the code and configuration in this repository: the
Python pipeline in `src/`, `scripts/` and `tools/`, the front end in
`web/index.html` and its CSS/JS, the tests, and the CI workflows.

It does NOT cover the three carve-outs below. Two of them are not mine to
license, and the third is licensed separately on purpose.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 1 — PROSE AND ANALYSIS: CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    docs/
    README.md
    CONTRIBUTING.md
    data/DATA.md
    session-summary/

The written analysis — methodology, findings, decision records — is licensed
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International, not MIT. See `LICENSE-docs`.

MIT is a software licence and reads as nonsense applied to a findings document.
CC BY is the one that carries the terms this work actually needs: credit the
source, and say what you changed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 2 — OPEN GOVERNMENT DATA: NOT MINE TO LICENSE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    data/
    web/data/

Every data file in these directories is derived from public open-government
releases and remains subject to its upstream terms. I hold no copyright in
them and grant none.

  - City of Edmonton sources — Open Government Licence – City of Edmonton
    https://data.edmonton.ca/stories/s/City-of-Edmonton-Open-Data-Terms-of-Use/msh8-if28/

  - Government of Alberta sources — Open Government Licence – Alberta

  - Highway reference geometry — © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Both Open Government Licences permit redistribution of derived works with
attribution, which is why these files can be committed here at all. Per-file
provenance, including which source each derives from, is in `data/DATA.md`.

If you reuse this data you inherit the attribution obligation directly from
those licences — it does not pass through me. The prescribed OGL attribution
statement, which is verbatim compliance text and must not be reworded, is
carried on the live site and pinned by
`tools/profiling/verify-about.js`.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CARVE-OUT 3 — VENDORED THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    web/vendor/

Third-party JS/CSS committed unmodified, under their own upstream licences:
maplibre-gl 4.7.1 (BSD-3-Clause) and deck.gl 9.0.38 (MIT, Urban Computing
Foundation). Versions, upstream URLs and SHA-256 provenance are in
`web/vendor/README.md`.

================================================================================

The carve-out paths above are the authoritative list. `tests/test_license.py`
reads them out of this file and fails if a data-shaped file is committed
outside them — a new data directory that nobody adds here would otherwise be
silently swept under the MIT grant.
